# Scripts
# These are tracked. `/scripts/*` used to ignore the lot as throwaway seeds, but
# they stopped being that: wiki-sweep retains every sweep-*.mjs precisely so a
# past run's reasoning stays readable, update-*/fix-* carry the same record for
# one-off corrections, and the DB tooling those runs are written against
# (maintenance-log, check-links, mark-verified, seed-utils) is infrastructure.
# Ignored, they lived on one machine's disk with no history behind them.
# Every one of them reads its credentials from process.env; none is hardcoded.
# Only their byproducts stay out, since those are not source: generated data
# manifests, and .backups/, which holds gzipped DB dumps (8.5 MB at run 320).
/scripts/*.json
/scripts/.backups/
CLAUDE.md

